  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Shoot and save in pairs",
  "description": "In pairs with one ball. Set out two cone goals facing each other, about 6 metres wide and 10 metres apart. One player shoots from their goal at their partner's goal, and the partner is the keeper and tries to save it. Then swap: the one who saved shoots back.\n\nChange the distance to suit – further away means harder shots, closer means more goals. Keep score and see who gets to five first. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Look up and pick a corner – then watch the ball as you strike it."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Lock your ankle: toes down, heel up."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "As keeper: stand ready on your toes with your hands in front of you."
    }
  ],
